#. Tag: title
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The input file is an ini-style configuration file (specifically, it is in "
"the format supported by the KConfig framework) that describes a set of "
"widgets. It contains a <literal>[Global]</literal> section, providing "
"general information about the plugin, and a section for each widget that "
"should be included in the plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <literal>[Global]</literal> section can have the following entries:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "DefaultGroup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default value for the <varname>Group</varname> entry in the class "
"sections (default: \"<literal>Custom</literal>\", unless the <option>-g</"
"option> option is given)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Includes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A (comma-separated) list of required includes (default: empty). Note that "
"the header files for the widgets specified later in file should not be "
"listed here; instead, this is for special headers for the plugin's own use, "
"like those for classes providing previews."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "PluginName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the main C++ class in the plugin (default: "
"\"<literal>WidgetsPlugin</literal>\", unless the <option>-n</option> option "
"is given)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each class should have its own <literal>[<replaceable>ClassName</"
"replaceable>]</literal> section, which can include the following entries:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "CodeTemplate"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value returned by the <code>codeTemplate()</code> function of the "
"plugin, which is marked for \"future use\" by &Qt; Designer (default: empty)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "ConstructorArgs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The arguments to pass to the constructor of the class given by "
"<literal>ImplClass</literal>; these must be surrounded by parentheses "
"(default: \"<literal>(parent)</literal>\"). The only variable guaranteed to "
"be available is <varname>parent</varname>, which is the parent "
"<code>QWidget</code> passed by &Qt; Designer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:210 man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "This entry is ignored if <literal>CreateWidget</literal> is set."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "CreateWidget"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The code necessary to create an instance of the widget (default: uses "
"<code>new</code> to create an instance of the class given by the "
"<literal>ImplClass</literal> entry, passing the arguments specified by "
"<literal>ConstructorArgs</literal>). See the notes for <literal>ImplClass</"
"literal> and <literal>ConstructorArgs</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "DomXML"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An XML UI description of the widget (default: the default provided by the "
"&Qt; Designer plugin headers)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The group to display the widget under in &Qt; Designer (default: the value "
"of the <varname>DefaultGroup</varname> entry in the <literal>[Global]</"
"literal> section)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "IconName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The image file or standard icon name to use as the icon for this widget in "
"the &Qt; Designer widget list (default: a PNG file named with the section "
"name, with any double colons removed, in the \"pics\" directory of a "
"compiled-in resource file; for example, <filename>:/pics/Foo.png</filename> "
"in the section <literal>[Foo]</literal>, or <filename>:/pics/FooBar.png</"
"filename> in the section <literal>[Foo::Bar]</literal>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "ImplClass"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The class that should be used to create an instance of the widget for the "
"use of &Qt; Designer (default: the section name). Note that this does not "
"actually have to be the class that would be created for an end application: "
"that is determined by the <literal>DomXML</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "IncludeFile"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The header that needs to be included to use this widget (default: the "
"lowercase version of the section name, with any colons removed and \".h\" "
"appended; for example, <literal>foo.h</literal> in the section "
"<literal>[Foo]</literal>, or <literal>foobar.h</literal> in the section "
"<literal>[Foo::Bar]</literal>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "IsContainer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether this widget can contain other widgets (default: <literal>false</"
"literal>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "ToolTip"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tooltip to display when hovering over the widget in the widget list of "
"&Qt; Designer (default: the section name, with \" Widget\" appended; for "
"example, <literal>Foo Widget</literal> in the section <literal>[Foo]</"
"literal>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "WhatsThis"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The What's This text associated with the widget in &Qt; Designer (default: "
"the section name, with \" Widget\" appended; for example, <literal>Foo "
"Widget</literal> in the section <literal>[Foo]</literal>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The simplest description file might look like <screen language=\"ini\">\n"
"<![CDATA[\n"
"[Foo]\n"
"ToolTip=Displays foos\n"
"[Bar]\n"
"ToolTip=Bar editor\n"
"]]>\n"
"    </screen> Note that each class must have at least one key set "
"(<literal>ToolTip</literal> was used in this example), otherwise it will be "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually, you want to change at least the user-visible text, which means the "
"<literal>ToolTip</literal>, <literal>WhatsThis</literal> and <literal>Group</"
"literal> entries. Additionally, setting the plugin name can be a good idea "
"to prevent possible symbol clashes and not confuse debuggers (both the "
"debugger application and the person doing the debugging):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<![CDATA[\n"
"[Global]\n"
"PluginName=FooWidgets\n"
"DefaultGroup=Display\n"
"\n"
"[Foo]\n"
"ToolTip=Displays bears\n"
"WhatsThis=An image widget that displays dancing bears\n"
"\n"
"[Bar]\n"
"ToolTip=Bar editor\n"
"WhatsThis=An editor interface for bars for bears\n"
"Group=Editing\n"
"]]>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More complex files may be necessary if you have namespaced classes or extra "
"options that need supplying to constructors, for example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<![CDATA[\n"
"[Global]\n"
"PluginName=FooWidgets\n"
"DefaultGroup=Foo\n"
"\n"
"[Foo::Bar]\n"
"ToolTip=Displays bars\n"
"WhatsThis=A widget that displays bars in a particular way\n"
"IncludeFile=foo/bar.h\n"
"IconName=:/previews/bar.png\n"
"\n"
"[Foo::Baz]\n"
"IncludeFile=foo/baz.h\n"
"ConstructorArgs=(Foo::Baz::SomeOption, parent)\n"
"Group=Foo (Special)\n"
"IsContainer=true\n"
"IconName=:/previews/baz.png\n"
"]]>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes especially complex widgets might need a special \"preview class\" "
"implementation for use in &Qt; Designer; this might be a subclass of the "
"real widget that just does some extra setup, or it might be a completely "
"different implementation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: man-kgendesignerplugin.1.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<![CDATA[\n"
"[Global]\n"
"Includes=foopreviews.h\n"
"\n"
"[FancyWidget]\n"
"ImplClass=FancyWidgetPreview\n"
"]]>"
msgstr ""

